  "title": "Provider-neutral work-tracker seam + GitHub adapter",
  "summary": "Adds a new `work_tracker` module to the osf crate: a provider-neutral `WorkTracker` trait (read items, write state, write recap, report capabilities) with its data types, a pure 'Ready' dispatch rule, a run-finishing helper that checks capabilities before writing state then recap, and an in-memory fake double. On top of that seam it adds the first real adapter, `github_work_tracker`, which drives GitHub Issues and Projects v2 through the `gh` CLI: pure argv/payload builders, pure response parsers, a `RealGhRunner` with timeout and explicit-token identity, and a refusal to write without an explicit builder identity. Three integration tests pin the fake run, the provider-neutrality of the seam, and the real runner's process behaviour.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
